A working vocabulary for contamination and cleanliness (@cm-vocabulary: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Contamination-Control-Engineering-NASA.lingua#r_2XKKPYTW2DPQPQZ8VPV23BJ8A5", #source "../sources/Sterile-Products-WHO.lingua#r_6BVEG1GSVGGGD566CJKD254DSB", #clean-manufacturing "A-process-map-for-unwanted-material.lingua#r_3HDYXGSDA5NAR504BAWK57VBQD") { r_0ZVPAQR75W9W44NBA2SJ0Z02AV
**Read:** [Contamination control engineering — Tribble and colleagues, NASA CR 4740](../sources/Contamination-Control-Engineering-NASA.lingua#r_2XKKPYTW2DPQPQZ8VPV23BJ8A5), definitions; [Sterile pharmaceutical products — WHO TRS 1044, Annex 2](../sources/Sterile-Products-WHO.lingua#r_6BVEG1GSVGGGD566CJKD254DSB), glossary. Compare the use of a term with its application.

Contamination, contaminação, is unwanted material in a specified context. Cleanliness, limpeza or grau de limpeza, describes a state relative to a requirement. Cleaning, limpeza as an operation, changes that state. A particle, partícula, is a discrete piece of matter; residue, resíduo, can include particles or a film. An aerosol, aerossol, consists of particles or droplets suspended in a gas.

Sampling, amostragem, obtains observations from only part of a target. Detection, detecção, and identification, identificação, answer different questions. Bioburden, carga microbiana, requires a stated recovery and enumeration method. Sterilization, esterilização, is not a synonym for removing all chemical residues.

**Work:** Build a bilingual glossary tied to your two objects. Include a physical example, an observable quantity and a counterexample for each term. Where a translation is ambiguous, retain the source's definition rather than treating the word alone as a specification.

